    {
      "id": "mlddugt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) and Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945) were prominent leaders in India's independence movement.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) and Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858) represent key revolutionary figures from different eras of resistance.",
        "The nationalist trio Lal-Bal-Pal consists of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were essential post-independence era builders."
      ],
      "id": "n7ejnok"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l35yv09",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of the Nation'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l5kyycr",
      "content": "• Leader of the Indian National Movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b2b8a8c",
      "content": "• Introduced Satyagraha and non-violent resistance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gviwk8r",
      "content": "• Led Non-Cooperation (1920), Civil Disobedience (1930), Quit India (1942)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wj2qrc6",
      "content": "• Led the Dandi March in 1930."
    },
    {
      "id": "cubqjqi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dgyo28k",
      "content": "• Popularly known as Netaji."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x3pvr8z",
      "content": "• Founded the Indian National Army (INA)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jm5n9c4",
      "content": "• Gave the slogan 'Give me blood and I will give you freedom'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c0nr2md",
      "content": "• Formed the Azad Hind Government."
    },
    {
      "id": "5udj3t0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9yzmzok",
      "content": "• Famous revolutionary freedom fighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0ed42yp",
      "content": "• Involved in the Lahore Conspiracy Case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b841wu5",
      "content": "• Along with Batukeshwar Dutt threw bombs in the Central Legislative Assembly in 1929."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zghf7lr",
      "content": "• Executed by the British in 1931."
    },
    {
      "id": "rrt95am",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q089ex9",
      "content": "• Queen of Jhansi and leader in the Revolt of 1857."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ba0cpmd",
      "content": "• Fought bravely against British forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "m3fvlzk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7gc2tsh",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of Indian Unrest'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mdnqwcq",
      "content": "• Gave slogan 'Swaraj is my birthright and I shall have it'."
    },
    {
      "id": "liwzk24",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lpul69f",
      "content": "• Known as 'Punjab Kesari'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lqil716",
      "content": "• Leader of Lal-Bal-Pal trio."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9yr86u4",
      "content": "• Died after injuries during Simon Commission protest."
    },
    {
      "id": "39ge1oi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y0p9b0r",
      "content": "• Member of Lal-Bal-Pal."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ii9tl7d",
      "content": "• Promoted the Swadeshi Movement."
    },
    {
      "id": "1crhdis",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fuz50ae",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Iron Man of India'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aeqrtai",
      "content": "• Integrated princely states after independence."
    },
    {
      "id": "0mae11d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c8ciacp",
      "content": "• Important Congress leader."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rt47h92",
      "content": "• First Prime Minister of India."
    },
